    926  fb32							; ==============================================================================
    927  fb32							; PhVcApplyOR / PhVcApplyAND DELETED (2026-10-19) — same retired vcrunch
    928  fb32							; tramp path. PhHcrEntry now stores the prefix mask directly (fixed 10).
    929  fb32							; ==============================================================================
    930  fb32							; ==============================================================================
    931  fb32							; HcrClock — hcrunch animation clock (fixed full=10 since 2026-10-19).
    932  fb32							;   In:  X = full extent (cells, ≥1); reads EnemyRamP (StartFrame-pinned)
    933  fb32							;   Out: A = covered (1..full) — never 0 (always-solid stub)
    934  fb32							;   Clobbers A (X/Y preserved — unlike CrunchClock). No latch: the kill
    935  fb32							;   repeats on contact (DropArm respawns at the room top, so no loop).
    936  fb32							; s = EnemyRamP>>4 (0..15, one 256f period = 16 buckets of 16f):
    937  fb32							;   s 0-3   dwell at home  (eff 0)	  -> n=1, 64f stub
    938  fb32							;   s 4-12  grow to center  (eff s-3)	  -> n 2..full (1..9 cells of
    939  fb32							;	    8px — full=w>>1; w=20 record = center of the screen)
    940  fb32							;   s 13-15 fast retract    (eff 3*(15-s) = 6,3,0) — wipe home in 3
    941  fb32							;	    steps (the old instant far-end turn, stretched to center)
    942  fb32							; covered = 1 + min(eff, full-1). CrunchClock (sc>>2 triangle, ~4f/step)
    943  fb32							; stays for its VCR mirrors + verify_build token gate — only the two
    944  fb32							; hcrunch call sites moved here (16f/step, grow-to-center ruling
    945  fb32							; 2026-10-16). Both callers pass full=10 (PhHcrEntry stages it, HOV
    946  fb32							; tests it); the latch freeze was removed with the 2026-10-19 contract.
    947  fb32							; ==============================================================================
    948  fb32							; PARKED (user 2026-10-28: "HCrunch should stop (retracted) when it kills the player.
    949  fb32							; It keeps moving and killing him again and again", then "still restarts after a
    950  fb32							; while"). LoseLife arms Hover ($FF) and DropArm drops him back to the SAME spot while
    951  fb32							; this clock kept running, so the prefix was extended again on arrival. Two parks:
    952  fb32							;   * Hover set (any death in this room): held retracted until his first thrust;
    953  fb32							;   * EnemyDeadMask b7 = crunch SPENT: a hcrunch kill sets it (.HFkill) and it stays
    954  fb32							;     retracted for the rest of the visit - EnterRoom clears the mask, so the crunch
    955  fb32							;     cycles again the next time he enters the room (or after a game-over reload).
    956  fb32							; Parked = n=1 (clock pinned at 0); the kill test skips while parked too.
    957  fb32				   HcrClock
