   1177  fd3c							; --- Phase 3: phase-cell blink (PF buffer pokes) ----------------------
   1178  fd3c							; Body moved after the level data (PhaseBlink, ~130B — the StageBandTab
   1179  fd3c							; window $F3C4..$F4C4 was full; the data window has the only free
   1180  fd3c							; hole). Contract: clobbers A/X/Y/FetchPtr/RectCount/LineCount/
   1181  fd3c							; CollisionCellX/CollisionEndY ($8F scratch — the pack below rebuilds
   1182  fd3c							; it). The PF buffers ARE the collision map (cell walk + laser read
   1183  fd3c							; them) — toggling the cell's two bits THERE makes render + PHM +
   1184  fd3c							; laser follow with zero kernel cost. 64f full cycle = EnemyRamP bit5
   1185  fd3c							; (32 on + 32 off; clock-derived, no state bytes — locked plan).
   1186  fd3c							; --- PhaseBlink ping-pong (chunk A2): it MUST run after the band/ball
   1187  fd3c							; staging above and before the pack below (the crunch walk overwrites
   1188  fd3c							; Temp/BandTab for its cell — running it earlier let SBT's own staging
   1189  fd3c							; erase the crunch mask, and every crunch kill stopped latching).
