   1195  fd3f							; --- Phase 4: pack collision overlay byte → CollisionEndY ($8F) ---
   1196  fd3f							; b4-b7 = right_col+1, b0-3 = the four ball band gates, 0 = symmetric.
   1197  fd3f							; When NO band is gated, b3 carries the M1-present flag instead, so an
   1198  fd3f							; M1-ONLY room still packs nonzero (the kernel's OverlayTramp gates on
   1199  fd3f							; LineCount != 0 — no M1 cross otherwise). The two uses cannot collide:
   1200  fd3f							; with a gate set, OvShutBand's mask comes from OvHead/OvTail, and a
   1201  fd3f							; player box in band 3 matches b3 only when a band-3 strip is drawn.
   1202  fd3f							; Cave never writes $8F; bank1 HUD entry copies it to LineCount ($84 —
   1203  fd3f							; cave .Row clobbers it) before overscan PHM reads. BallX in Temp stays
   1204  fd3f							; raw (the kernel's ball block reads it later this VBL).
   1205  fd3f							; Gate mask, rebuilt from the same two metas (PhaseBlink sits between the
   1206  fd3f							; staging and this pack and clobbers every other VBL scratch byte).
   1207  fd3f							; Temp = 0 means the room has NO ball column, so every gate is off —
   1208  fd3f							; that also keeps a DOOR room's MetaA b0 (the m1_right flag) from
   1209  fd3f							; reading as a band-0 gate.
